\par\par \b \uc2 WEEKAHEAD-View from editors in the Americas\b0\par\par\uc2 883 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2011\par 23:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 28 (Reuters) - Following is the view from editors in the Americas on the top stories for the week ahead:\par \par \uc2 HIGHLIGHTS:\par \par \uc2 * ECONOMIC DATA: U.S payroll report\par \par \uc2 * MARKETS: Jitters on Egypt unrest\par \par \uc2 * EARNINGS: Oil, pharma, media reports\par \par \uc2 Watch the Weekahead on Reuters Insider:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://bit.ly/ekIvJ5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://bit.ly/ekIvJ5}}}\par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC DATA\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Labor Department has made a habit of disappointing Wall Street lately. In three of the last four monthly employment reports, the jobs tally fell short of economists' expectations. Friday's data for January offers an opportunity for redemption. A preliminary Reuters poll of economists shows they are looking for a gain of 150,000 jobs in January, which would be an improvement over the 103,000 reported in December. As for that December number, watch for any revisions. The Labor Department revised up its job count for five consecutive months starting in July. ADP's private payrolls data comes two days earlier. This is its first monthly report since wrong-footing markets by reporting a huge December jobs gain that looked nothing like the Labor Department's. Also on tap are personal income data on Monday, which includes the Federal Reserve's favorite inflation gauge. Tuesday brings January manufacturing sector data, followed by the much-larger services sector on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Turmoil in Egypt is unlikely to be quelled quickly, so markets will open Monday with fresh reaction to events over the weekend. Equities, particularly energy shares, may face pressure again while safe havens, including Treasuries and the dollar, could see renewed vigor. Emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the euro will still be under pressure. The stock market will wade through a further slew of earnings and Friday's payroll report, if solid, should help stocks. In the municipal market, eyes will be on New York's budget to see how lawmakers plan to close an approximate $10 billion gap.\par \par \uc2 OIL/ENERGY RESULTS\par \par \uc2 Exxon Mobil\uc2 , the world's largest listed company, leads the quarterly updates from the energy sector, following news of stronger profits from the likes of \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , \uc2 ConocoPhillips\uc2  and Occidental. (See story at [ID: nN28275236]). Exxon is expected to say it scored massive quarterly profits lifted by the strength in oil prices, but it will have to convince investors that its big bet on North American natural gas will pay off in the years to come. Other energy giants including \uc2 Marathon Oil Corp\uc2 , \uc2 Anadarko Petroleum\uc2  and coal producer \uc2 Massey Energy\uc2  will also report, as will the largest U.S. maker of chemicals, \uc2 Dow Chemical\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BERNANKE FACES REPORTERS\par \par \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve officials hit the speech circuit after their latest decision to stay the course with their $600 billion bond-buying plan. Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke stages a rare question and answer session with journalists after a speech on Thursday, which will be closely parsed for clues on how patient the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be as the economy builds its strength. The Fed has been mulling holding regular news conferences: could this be a warm up? On Friday, Dallas Fed chief Richard Fisher, an inflation hawk who rotated into a voting seat on the Fed's policy panel this year, will explain why he defied type and backed QE2. Minneapolis Fed's Narayana Kocherlakota, a centrist, speaks on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 MEDIA/PHARMA EARNINGS\par \par \uc2 The media sector reporting season cranks up with \uc2 News Corp\uc2  and \uc2 Time Warner\uc2  on Wednesday and \uc2 Viacom\uc2  on Thursday. All face questions about advertising's fate as video streaming grows. Merck on Tuesday and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  a day later top the list of "Big Pharma" names detailing quarterly results. For them, the big issue is likely to be price pressure as it was in \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 's results this past week. In finance, Visa and \uc2 MasterCard\uc2  - both furiously lobbying for an easing in the Fed rules on interchange fees - will report on Wednesday and Thursday, respectively. Finally, \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2 , the world's largest package delivery company, will provide a snapshot on Tuesday of fourth-quarter economic activity.\par \par \uc2 MEXICAN PESO\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will begin publishing minutes from its monetary policy meetings on Friday, raising questions about whether the more transparent approach will affect volatility in Mexican assets. Investors will be watching for any signs of concern about the strength of the peso although President Felipe Calderon has said no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is planned, setting \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  apart from many other countries in Latin America which are trying an array of measures to curb their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CANADA\par \par \uc2 In Canada, Friday's employment data is expected to show the economy added just 16,000 jobs in January, down from a revised 30,400 in December. Further confirmation the recovery is intact but sluggish should also be found in Monday's monthly GDP data for November, which is forecast to rise 0.3 percent from a month earlier. Elsewhere, the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  will offer fresh clues on its thinking in two speeches by Senior Deputy Governor Tiff Macklem. TAKE A LOOK-Five world markets themes next week [MKT/THEMES] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Weekahead Europe [WKAHEAD/EM]     Weekahead Asia [WKAHEAD/A]\par Economic events [M/DIARY]          Company news [GLO/EQUITY]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For all diaries [DIA]\f28 \par \par \uc2 WEEKAHEAD/AMERICAS|LANGEN|Table|G|RBN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|PGE    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110128e71s00200\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
