\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real up on minutes,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2011\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real adds 0.2 pct after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  minutes\par \par \uc2 * Bank seen stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via swaps, forwards\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso up 0.4 pct, Mexican peso flat\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Jan 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, pushed higher on Thursday after minutes from the country's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting indicated further interest rate hikes in the months ahead.\par \par \uc2 Rising prices are likely to force Brazil to keep increasing its benchmark interest rate, which would attract more foreign investment and boost the already overvalued local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.24 percent stronger at 1.665 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market in early trading, getting closer to the 1.65-per-dollar level which could prompt more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, higher copper prices pushed up the Chilean peso but Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggled to break free of the key 12-per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 "The minutes (from Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting) showed even more interest rate hikes. The long end of the interest rate futures curve is continuing to rise, which shows the market is beginning to prepare for a longer tightening cycle," said Andre Ferreira, director of the Futura Corretora brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "That will end up bringing more dollars to the market," he added.\par \par \uc2 In the minutes from last week's rate-setting meeting, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would require "prompt corrections" to bring inflation back on target. [ID:nN27240799]\par \par \uc2 At that meeting, policy-makers raised Brazil's benchmark interest rate by 50 basis points to 11.25 percent and indicated further hikes were to come.\par \par \uc2 But the real's gains could force the authorities to take even more aggressive action in the market to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation and protect local manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 "We'll see two auctions today for sure," said Futura's Ferreira, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily purchases of dollars in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also later announce another reverse swap auction, which has the same effect as buying dollars in the futures market, or even call its first forwards auction. [ID:nN25294325]\par \par \uc2 COPPER RISE BOOSTS PESO\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=>, which has also become a source of concern for the country's authorities, firmed 0.43 percent to 486.7 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was boosted as the price of copper, the country's main export and economic lifeline, rose on supply worries. [ID:nLDE70Q1B6]\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Chile announced a record $12 billion in dollar purchases during 2011. The government has said it will also invest its military copper funds abroad and look to increase local financing of foreign businesses in an effort to ease pressure on the peso. [ID:nN26126403]\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> was flat at 11.99 per dollar in early trading, struggling to definitively break the 12-per-dollar level.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's non-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance has made the peso a relatively attractive bet in the region but the 12-per-dollar level has proved to be a strong barrier of resistance. ( Editing by W Simon )\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110130e71r00071\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
