\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico's peso dips on official's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  talk\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2011\par 16:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexico finance minister says govt is eyeing peso gains\par \par \uc2 * Comments increase market bets on more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Analysts doubt any Mexican action is imminent\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso down 0.24 pct, Chile peso dips 0.2 pct (Updates prices, adds background)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Jan 25 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso weakened on Tuesday after the country's finance minister said the government was eyeing the peso's recent ascent, raising concerns in the market that Mexican authorities could increase \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts doubted \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on the verge of wading deeper into the so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war that has drawn an increasing number of economies to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or enact capital controls as they seek to protect their exporters from surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mexican Finance Minister Ernesto Cordero said on Tuesday that the government was "paying a lot of attention" to the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation but he did not think controls on capital inflows would be appropriate for Mexico. [ID:nLDE70O1KC]\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts have been speculating that Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could increase the $600 million in dollar put options it is selling every month.\par \par \uc2 "Businessmen are complaining the strong peso could affect competitiveness, and authorities could start buying more dollars to break the appreciation a bit," said Antonio Magana, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Interacciones in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The options program is a less aggressive measure than those that have been taken by other emerging economies to fight strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have been inflated by flows from yield-hungry foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 Still, a move to increase the program could spur temporary losses in the peso, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 But many analysts think the peso will have to mount even stronger gains before authorities could decide to take action.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained around 4 percent from a November intraday low, helped by an improving outlook for the closely-linked U.S. and Mexican economies.\par \par \uc2 WHAT, ME WORRY?\par \par \uc2 Even if exporters are grumbling about getting less pesos for their exports, the government is not feeling the pressure as a surge in oil prices is generating a windfall in government revenue from crude oil sales sales, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "We have surplus peso revenue due to the level of oil prices, despite the exchange rate," said Salvador Orozco, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt strategist at Santander in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Mexico gets about one-third of its revenue from oil sales by the state-run monopoly. Congress set the 2011 budget with a $65.40 per barrel estimate for Mexican crude prices, but the market the price for the country's blend <MEX-OSP> has climbed to just below $84 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 "I do not think the government will worry if (the peso) gets to 11.80 (per dollar) ... If it goes to 11 (per dollar), maybe there would be distortions," Orozco added.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=> bid 0.2 percent weaker at 492.70 as investors worried that rising interest rates in emerging economies like China would dampen demand demand for copper, the countries top export.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's local market was closed for a holiday, but the real <BRL=> bid almost flat, edging 0.03 percent firmer in international trade at 1.6708 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110128e71p001h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
