\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  narrowly mixed; Brazil real flat\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2011\par 14:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil real up 0.06 pct after interest rate hike\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso slumps 0.45 pct as copper price falls\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso rises 0.15 pct on U.S. housing data (Adds comments and context, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Moises Avila\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Jan 20 (Reuters) - Brazil's real edged firmer on Thursday after the country raised interest rates as expected for the first time since July, but investors were cautious of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to crimp the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso firmed after U.S. housing data beat expectations and Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped on concerns China could tighten borrowing costs and hit demand for copper, the country's main export.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its benchmark interest rate by 50 basis points to 11.25 percent late on Wednesday. For details, see [ID:nN19215154]\par \par \uc2 Although economists say higher borrowing costs are necessary to curb a worrying surge in inflation, the move is likely to attract even more investors to Brazil chasing higher yields and push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fresh highs.\par \par \uc2 "People think interest rates could go up even more," said Carlos Gandolfo, a partner at Sao Paulo's Pioneer brokerage.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.06 percent stronger at 1.670 per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has been using an array of measures to tame a rally in the real, which has gained about 13 percent since last May. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would call a reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction on Friday, its latest mechanism to reel in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nN20147163]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would take other measures beside interest rate hikes to try to cool inflation, such as a recent increase in bank reserve requirements.\par \par \uc2 "The tightening cycle will be smaller than the market was imagining," Andre Perfeito, an economist with Gradual Investimentos in Sao Paulo, said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Investors pared back bets on the size of future interest rate hikes, pushing down yields on short-dated interest rate futures contracts <0#DIJ:>.\par \par \uc2 MEXICO UP, CHILE DOWN\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> firmed 0.15 percent to 12.0675 per dollar, helped by data that showed U.S. existing home sales rose more than expected in December.\par \par \uc2 "The home sales data came out very strong ... this indicates that the United States (economy) is doing better than expected. This is helping us," said Omar Martin del Campo, a trader at Ve por Mas, a bank in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week hit its strongest level in more than two years and it has gained more than 4 percent since a November low on the improving economic outlook for the United States, which buys most of Mexico's exports.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled back from early losses that took it to its weakest in five sessions on fears that China could tighten monetary policy also crimp global growth.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> bid 0.45 percent weaker at 494.20 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, fell sharply.\par \par \uc2 A slowing of the Chinese economy could reduce its demand for raw materials, hurting the economies of commodity-producing Latin American countries. [ID:nTOE70J02S]\par \par \uc2 "What is weighing most are the declines by European stocks and the negative effect of lower commodity prices, such as copper," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Mining stocks dragged European markets down, on the assumption that demand for basic resources would fall if China's growth is reined in. [ID:nLDE70J0E3]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110123e71k0007f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
