\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real firms, helped by rate hike bets\b0\par\par\uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2011\par 17:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso retreats after break below 12/dlr\par \par \uc2 * Easing euro zone worries support region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real up 0.3 pct, Chile's peso up 0.2 pct (Updates to afternoon)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Sean Mattson\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Jan 18 (Reuters) - Brazil's real firmed on Tuesday ahead of an expected interest rate hike, while Mexico's peso retreated after breaking the psychological 12 per dollar barrier for the first time since late 2008.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to raise interest rates on Wednesday helped the real to outperform the region. For more, see: [ID:nSPG003198]\par \par \uc2 Brazil has been reluctant to raise its already high borrowing costs for fear of attracting even more short-term, speculative money. The Brazilian real <BRBY> was bid 0.3 percent stronger at 1.676 per dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 Rising inflation has made an interest rate hike seem inevitable. While the consensus among economists and market participants is for a 50-basis-point rise, the market has also partially priced in a 75-basis-point increase.\par \par \uc2 "(A) recent surge in food commodity prices ... could aggravate the situation further and could further deteriorate inflation expectations," Zeina Latif, chief Brazil economist at RBS in Sao Paulo, said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Rising investor sentiment in Germany and signs that policymakers will eventually firm up plans to ease the euro zone's debt crisis helped support riskier assets worldwide and weakened the dollar. [ID:nLDE70H0UU] [ID:nLDE70H0DQ]\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> also firmed 0.2 percent to 490.20 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, rose because of the weak dollar. [ID:nLDE70H0DP]\par \par \uc2 PESO PULLBACK\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> weakened 0.51 percent to 12.0325 per dollar as investors took profits after the peso broke below the key 12-per-dollar level on Monday for the first time since a steep devaluation in October 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso, which has lagged the gains in other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , strengthened more than 5 percent from a November intraday low to Tuesday's session high boosted by an improving outlook for U.S. and Mexican growth.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like a good opportunity to lock in some of the gains," said Marjorie Hernandez, an analyst at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York, who expected the peso to firm back toward 11.80 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The underlying story hasn't changed. It's still a great macro call for the year, people believe the U.S. is going to recover, it's still cheap, and they still aren't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she added.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been supported by flows from investors looking for a haven from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics of other central banks.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso is barely clawing back toward its pre-crisis levels, but analysts say Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could move to increase a program under which it is selling $600 million of dollar put options every month to local banks.\par \par \uc2 Luis Flores, an analyst at brokerage IXE in Mexico City, said a bigger options program would still be seen "as a more patient and subtle" reaction compared with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanisms in Chile, Brazil and Turkey. The shock of the announcement could derail peso gains, but "only for a matter of days," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Fundamentally it will not remove the favorable tendency for the peso," Flores said.\par \par \uc2 The options allow local banks to sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a slightly preferential rate when the peso has been on a winning streak and is below a 20-day moving average. By sucking up dollars directly from banks, policymakers can keep some dollar off the open market.\par \par \uc2 Gabriel Casillas, an analyst at \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  in Mexico City, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take a bolder move to begin daily dollar purchases if further peso gains take the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly and significantly below 12 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "This would still be a market-friendly mechanism -- relative to capital control measures that other countries have recently adopted -- and could reduce the speed of appreciation of the peso," Casillas wrote in a report. (Writing by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|ABX|BNX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110121e71i00191\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
