\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Closes Weaker; USD/MXN Back Above 12\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2011\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso closed weaker Tuesday as participants took some profits following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first close below MXN12 to the U.S. dollar since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN12.0330, according to Infosel, compared with MXN11.9945 at the close Monday. The move back above MXN12, seen as an important psychological level for the peso, came as the dollar ceded ground against other majors.\par \par \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  lowered the stop on its recommendation to buy pesos against a 65% dollar/35% euro basket. "By most metrics, MXN continues to stand out as fair-to-slightly undervalued at a time when many other [emerging market] \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appear significantly over-valued," RBC said in a report.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, RBC sees little likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the peso as "Mexican policy makers seem willing to accept gradual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation and reject implementing taxes/controls on capital."\par \par \uc2 Bank of America/Merrill Lynch echoed that view in a report, citing commitment to a free-floating regime, a still competitive exchange rate reflected in narrowing external deficits, and tolerance for some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength among authorities.\par \par \uc2 While Mexico's inclusion in \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's World Government Bond Index makes capital controls highly unlikely, other \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  options would also be of dubious effect, BofA/Merrill said in a report.\par \par \uc2 With the size of the peso market--globally $50 billion a day according to the 2010 Bank of International Settlements survey--a dollar-buying program would have to be large to affect the exchange rate, and include discretionary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BofA/Merrrill said. Currently, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys up to $600 million a month under a system of put options that can be exercised when the peso is stronger than its 20-day average.\par \par \uc2 BofA/Merrill said a cut in the Bank of Mexico's overnight interest rate target from the current 4.5%, which has been among points of speculation, could even be counterproductive and encourage more investment flows. "Yields in short-term bills (Cetes) and implied yields in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards are already trading below the 4.5% policy rate given excess local liquidity, and this has yet to discourage investors," the investment bank said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on benchmark 28-day Cetes fell by seven basis points at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's primary auction Tuesday to 4.13%.\par \par \uc2 Rodrigo Barros Reyes, the Finance Ministry's director of public policy analysis, said at a U.N. press event that the government doesn't see the peso's appreciation as a threat to Mexico's 2011 economic growth outlook, which has been revised upward by a number of economists in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 "The central scenario is that the economy will see good growth rates in 2011, even incorporating the trend of capital inflows that has led the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slightly stronger levels," Barros said.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980-5176, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Paul Kiernan contributed to this article. [ 18-01-11 2140GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \p