\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Steps countries are taking to counter hot money\b0\par\par\uc2 1,179 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 10:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Jan 10 (Reuters) - More governments around the world are moving to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening or control the flow of money into their economies as investors pour money into higher-yielding markets, turning their backs on low interest rates in developed economies.\par \par \uc2 Below are recent cases of direct or indirect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, compiled by Reuters:\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL TARGETS SHORT-SELLERS, HOPING TO WEAKEN REAL\par \par \uc2 * Brazil made its boldest move so far to curb gains in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , imposing on Thursday reserve requirements on banks' short positions on U.S. dollars in a bid to reduce speculative trade that has pushed the real near two-year highs.\par \par \uc2 * The surprise move will make it more expensive for banks to bet against the dollar. Short positions on dollars, a bet the real will strengthen against the greenback, surged to the highest on record at the end of December.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nLDE7050Z6] [ID:nN06102054]\par \par \uc2 CHILE ANNOUNCES LONG-AWAITED \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces on Jan 4 it plans a record $12 billion in dollar purchases during 2011 to tame the strong peso. It stresses that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is exceptional, warns against "addiction" to it.\par \par \uc2 * Chilean President Sebastian Pinera says no plans for capital controls.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifts limits on pension funds' overseas investment.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN04206531] [ID:nN04221079]\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL BUYS DOLLARS, FIGHTS INFLOWS, LOOKS TO TAX BREAKS\par \par \uc2 * Aggressive measures promised by incoming President Rousseff on Dec 31 including targeted tariff increases and tax breaks to address effects of strong real <BRBY>.\par \par \uc2 * Raises bank reserve requirements on Dec 4 to cool a credit boom and ease the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation.\par \par \uc2 * Sovereign wealth fund authorized to buy dollars on spot market but has yet to act.\par \par \uc2 * Government triples tax on foreign purchases of bonds to 6 percent on Oct 18 to curb inflows into fixed income market.\par \par \uc2 * Government increases tax on derivatives margins to dissuade short-term investors.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN30113578] [ID:nN04214108] [ID:nN03188472]\par \par \uc2 PERU BUYS DOLLARS, ENCOURAGES INVESTMENT ABROAD\par \par \uc2 * On Dec 31 government trims average tariff on imports to 3.4 percent from 5 percent, possibly resulting in increased imports and less appreciation pressure on the sol <PEN=PE>.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys about $9 billion dollars on the spot market in 2010, equivalent to around 6 percent of GDP. The treasury also bought around $500 million.\par \par \uc2 * On Nov 26 banking regulator SBS says drawing up rule to curb use of short-term derivatives called non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) to limit pressure on the sol.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises deposit requirements on bank accounts, especially those tied to foreign loans, in a bid to limit speculation on the sol.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN26131354] [ID:Nn31130618]\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN TIGHTENS \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RULES\par \par \uc2 * Financial Supervisory Commission says on Dec 30 it will investigate bank trading to see whether foreign capital involved in speculation.\par \par \uc2 * On Dec 27 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped trading in non-deliverable forwards at one fifth of a bank's total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading.\par \par \uc2 * Tightened reserve requirements ratio for Taiwan dollar passbook deposits held by foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links [ID:nTOE6BR007] [ID:nTOE6BT02Q] [ID:nTOE6B200N]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA SET TO IMPOSE BANK LEVY, WITHHOLDING TAX\par \par \uc2 * Announces on Dec 20 a proposal to levy banks' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt from late 2011, expected to be at a level less than 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 * Government expected to reinstate withholding tax on local bond holdings by foreign investors' later this year, expected to be set at 14 percent.\par \par \uc2 * In June set ceilings on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives that banks can hold of 250 percent of equity capital for foreign bank branches and 50 percent for domestic banks. Says at end of December that these will be cut further to 200 and 40 percent respectively.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nTOE702015] [ID:nTOE6B6021] [ID:nSUL000219]\par \par \uc2 TURKEY UPS RESERVE REQUIREMENTS\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says on Dec 21 will use all tools in its policy arsenal to cap speculative inflows.\par \par \uc2 * Increases reserve requirements for banks' short term lira deposits, to prevent lira strengthening.\par \par \uc2 * Signals may also lift requirement for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits.\par \par \uc2 * Says not actively considering Tobin tax on hot money.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nLDE6BK0TQ] [ID:nWEA8613]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA EASES EXCHANGE CONTROLS\par \par \uc2 * South Africa eases exchange controls on Dec 14, allowing local institutions to invest more money abroad\par \par \uc2 * Government says it will build up foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to curb rand <ZAR=> appreciation.\par \par \uc2 * But analysts doubt it has financial muscle to force down rand; finance minister says international cooperation needed.\par \par \uc2 --Story links: [ID:nL3E6NE0FH] [ID:nLDE68F1ER]\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA SAYS TO CONTROL BANKS' FOREIGN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  HOLDINGS\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals on Dec 3 it will impose new measures to control inflows, including management of commercial banks' minimum reserve ratios in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank accounts and rupiah-denominated giro accounts held by foreigners with local banks.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced a minimum holding period of one month for its bills in June this year in a move to channel strong capital inflows away from short-term investments.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nL3E6N30LR][ID:nL3E6NA0BJ]\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINES RELAXES \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RULES IN RESPONSE TO INFLOWS\par \par \uc2 * On Nov 17 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it will use measures such as building up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and additional bank regulations to deal with foreign inflows.\par \par \uc2 * Approved six measures in late October, involving higher ceilings for residents' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases and outward investments, and encouraging foreign debt prepayments by the private sector -- moves aimed at encouraging outflows of capital and dampening a peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <PHP=PDSP> that has reached 2-year highs.\par \par \uc2 * Bank to stay active in market as peso <PHP=> rises.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nSGE6AG058][ID:nSGE69R0EK] [ID:nSGE69R0I4]\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA INTRODUCES DOLLAR PURCHASES, STRUCTURAL MEASURES\par \par \uc2 * Finance ministry says on Nov 17 it will only use external financing in 2011 to meet outside obligations to ease pressure on peso <COP=>.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says on Oct 29 buying at least $20 million daily until at least March 15.\par \par \uc2 * Government kept $1.5 billion abroad last year, which included $1.4 billion in government dividends from state oil firm \uc2 Ecopetrol\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Plans to possibly hedge up to $3.7 billion in external debt service payments in 2011.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN29291838] [ID:nN16108112] [ID:nN02213742]\par \par \uc2 THAILAND TAXES FOREIGN BOND INVESTORS\par \par \uc2 * Thailand imposes 15 pct withholding tax on interest and capital gains earned by foreign investors on Thai bonds from Oct 13, 2010.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says on Nov 24 would consider further measures including a Tobin-style tax on international transactions.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nL3E6MO0SA] [ID:nSGE69B0A6] [ID:nSGE6970DX]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  ESCHEWS \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 , PESO SET TO OUTPERFORM\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying $600 million per month by selling dollar put options as a means to build up its reserves.\par \par \uc2 * Says capital controls do not work.\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso <MXN=> lagged gains in other markets, yet to firm back to pre-crisis levels.\par \par \uc2 * Strategists see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures across Latin America boosting attraction of free-floating Mexican peso.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN10261374] [ID:nN15182353] (Compiled by Rachel Armstrong)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2 /CONTROLS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABN|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|D|E|RBN|I