\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latin American  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  dip on Portugal woes\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2011\par 14:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Fears over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in futures market weigh on real\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real loses 0.12 pct, Chile's peso dips 0.2 pct\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso firms 0.14, aided by less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments and updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, (Reuters) - Chile's peso and Brazil's real slipped Monday after concerns that Portugal may be the next European state to seek a bailout pushed investors to sell riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Pressure grew Monday on Portugal to follow in the footsteps of Greece and Ireland by seeking financial help from the European Union and International Monetary Fund. Some investors fear a widening debt crisis in Europe could weigh down global growth.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were largely tracking the euro, a key barometer used by investors to gauge overall risk appetite, traders said. Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared losses after the euro bounced off a four-month low.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real also suffered from concerns that the government could take further steps to control its recent appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The country's sovereign wealth fund was formally authorized Monday to operate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market while speculation about action in the futures market intensified.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was bid 0.12 percent weaker at 1.686 per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 "The expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could act in (the) derivatives (futures market) is reinforcing the global move. It's a mix of global moves and local noise," said Roberto Padovani, chief Brazil economist with WestLB bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 MEXICAN PESO ON SIDELINES\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso sank to a four-month low past the key 500-per-dollar level early Monday but snapped back to bid only 0.2 percent weaker at 498.50 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The 500-level is a level that a number of clients have mentioned where they would find the peso as attractive," said Rafael de la Fuente, an economist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in New York. "The economy is doing very well, it is fundamentally strong."\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso was hammered down about 6 percent last week from a near three-year high after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would buy $12 billion this year in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose strength is hurting exporters.\par \par \uc2 The market is divided about whether Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hike interest rates Thursday to cool rising inflation or if it could leave borrowing costs steady so as not to boost the attraction of its debt to yield-hungry investors.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Monday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan was working and that policymakers felt "independent" to move its benchmark rate according to the bank's inflation objectives.\par \par \uc2 "It is an interesting comment. I think they will hike, precisely because even though they have introduced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the risks to inflation are skewed to the upside," de la Fuente said.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed 0.14 percent to 12.2180 per dollar, backed by bets of stronger exports and less risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has yet to recover its strength since before the 2008 crisis and policymakers are not threatening to take any action.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the sidelines of this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war, like the Mexican peso, will be attractive in 2011," Luis Flores, an economist at brokerage IXE, wrote in a report.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also supported by an improving outlook for the economy in the United States, its top trading partner, as well as rising oil prices as Mexico's export blend trades around its highest price since Oct. 2008. (Additonal reporting by Brad Haynes in Santiago; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110113e71a00141\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
