\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico's peso posts 6 pct gain in 2010\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2010\par 23:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso firms almost 6 percent in 2010\par \par \uc2 * Slower growth seen cooling \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain in 2011\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatens other Latam \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Dec 31 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso firmed on Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  notched a nearly 6 percent gain for the year, boosted by a strong recovery in exports to top trading partner the United States.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> firmed to 12.3650 per U.S. dollar on Friday. Local markets in other major economies were closed for the New Year's eve holiday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect much weaker gains seen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Latin America against the dollar in the coming year as growth slows in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  and southern economies step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Investors should not extrapolate the Mexican peso's outperformance in 2010 to 2011," said Jimena Zuniga, an analyst at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Stronger than expected data and the extension of tax cuts in the United States pushed some analysts to revise up their forecasts for U.S. growth in 2010, but Zuniga points out that Mexico's economy will see slower growth next year compared to 2010, when it likely grew around 5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "Both the U.S. and Mexican economies had a lot of slack in 2010 to support growth, but the slack has diminished a lot in Mexico even if not so much in the United States," Zuniga said.\par \par \uc2 Low interest rates in major economies, which are trying to spur growth and underpin a recovery from the 2008 financial crisis, spurred high demand for Latin American debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2010, helping drive solid gains across the region. For details see [ID:nN30121533].\par \par \uc2 While yield-hungry investors starved by low U.S. rates will likely continue to pile into Latin American assets early in 2010, some analysts believe faster than expected growth in the United States could awaken expectations of a rate hike by the U.S. Federal Reserve toward the end of 2011.\par \par \uc2 "This could deter flow from foreign investors toward emerging markets, and we could even see outflows," wrote analysts at Santander, which expects the Mexican peso to weaken more than 2 percent to 12.70 per dollar by the end of 2011.\par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region could also see gains crimped by increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by officials who are concerned that strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are hurting local exporters and that foreign flows could be inflating bubbles in the region's assets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil and Colombia have mounted significant dollar buying programs by their central banks to contain gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Chile could soon join the fray if its peso gains much more ground, said \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' Zuniga.\par \par \uc2 "We envision more of this type of war between flows that are attracted to the market's fundamentals and the policy response by authorities," she said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed 2011 at a 31-month high as the domestic economy roared back from the devastation of an earthquake early in the year. [ID:nN30111514]\par \par \uc2 But slowing growth may lead the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a string of rate hikes in January, which could portend that policymakers are willing to pump up inflation by weakening the peso, Zuniga said. [ID:nN30111514]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110103e6cv000zf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
