\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real slips,  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso firms slightly\b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2010\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real hurt by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations\par \par \uc2 * Higher copper price helps support Chilean peso\par \par \uc2 * China rate hike fears, EU debt woes may weigh next week\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's real slipped on Friday, hurt by expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local authorities to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, while the Mexican peso edged up, helped by stronger than expected U.S. data.\par \par \uc2 The real closed 0.35 percent weaker at 1.713 on the local spot market <BRBY>, recording a 1.64 percent loss for the week.\par \par \uc2 Traders pointed to comments from Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega on Thursday that authorities could step up efforts to contain the real's gains, which are hurting exporters.\par \par \uc2 "After Mantega spoke yesterday, people became even more alert to the possibility that the government could act with more force in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Jose Carlos Amado, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Renascenca brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCB) has recently started calling two auctions a day, instead of just one, to buy U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 "With the USDBRL now close to 1.71, the BCB resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  once during the day, reinforcing our thesis that BCB becomes more aggressive below 1.70," wrote analysts at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> firmed to a fresh 30-month high in early trading but was later flat at 475.80 per dollar. The price of copper, the country's main export, pared early gains.\par \par \uc2 Chinese imports, including copper, soared in November while bank lending topped forecasts, suggesting the booming Chinese economy will continue to gobble up Latin American commodities such as Chilean copper and Brazilian soybeans.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 0.86 percent during the week.\par \par \uc2 CHINA, EUROPE LOOM\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> firmed 0.21 percent to 12.4505 per dollar after U.S. data consumer confidence to its highest level in six months and trade data showed that imports from Mexico rose to a record high in October. [ID:nN10163525]\par \par \uc2 Mexico sends around 80 percent of its exports to the United States and Latin America's No. 2 economy is counting on a firm recovery north of the border to support its own rebound from a deep recession.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso was on track to post a weekly loss of around 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be hurt by signs that China could soon move to hike interest rates. Chinese data on Saturday that is expected to show another pick-up in inflation.\par \par \uc2 "The intensity of the depreciation will depend on the comments that are made in China and the measures they take to keep the economy from overheating," said Mario Copca, an analyst at brokerage Vanguardia in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Further signs of trouble in Europe's debt crisis could also weigh next week.\par \par \uc2 EU heads of state and government meet on Dec. 16-17 to discuss the region's spreading debt crisis. Expectations of meaningful progress are low after Germany and France on Friday rejected calls for an increase in the bloc's rescue fund and joint sovereign bonds. [ID:nLDE6B90K3]\par \par \uc2 "There is going to be more noise from Europe ... the big risk is that Italy gets downgraded," Copca said. (Additional reporting by Jose de Castro in Sao Paulo and Lorena Segura in Mexico City; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101213e6ca000ui\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
