\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile and Mexico's  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm on US data\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2010\par 17:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Strong U.S. data raises hopes about export demand\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real weakens as dollar recovers worldwide\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso adds 0.3 pct, Chilean peso up 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warns of "big" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Adds comments about Colombia and \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Nov 5 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile and Mexico firmed on Friday after strong U.S. jobs data raised hopes about demand for both countries' exports.\par \par \uc2 But Brazil's real edged lower as the dollar recovered from sharp losses in the wake of U.S. stimulus measures.\par \par \uc2 Data showing the United States added more jobs than expected in October lifted hopes about the global recovery, boosting the price of many industrial metals. [ID:nN0528209]\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> gained 0.51 percent to 477.3 per dollar as the price of copper, the country's main export, hit a two-year high. For details, see [ID:nSGE6A4055]\par \par \uc2 Like many other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chile's peso has soared in recent months, putting pressure on the country's exporters.\par \par \uc2 After soaring as much as 2.1 percent on Thursday, the peso recorded a weekly gain of 2.5 percent, its biggest since May this year.\par \par \uc2 The peso barely budged after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday announced fresh measures to encourage outflows and ease the peso's recent rally. [ID:nN04221079]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the foreign investment limit for pension funds -- a measure analysts at Standard Chartered said should have little impact. "Tax breaks to encourage outbound investment may be required to sweeten the deal," they wrote in a note on Friday. [ID:nN04221079]\par \par \uc2 "The Chilean peso still appears to be one of the strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays in Latin America," they said.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> also fared slightly better thanks to improved U.S. jobs data. The United States buys about 80 percent of Mexico's exports. The peso is very sensitive to the changing outlook for the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The peso firmed 0.25 percent to 12.2015 per dollar and was heading for a weekly gain of 1.15 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe Mexico's hands-off approach to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will help boost the peso over coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be willing to take the appreciation as long as it's not in a very disordered fashion," said Italo Lombardi, a Latin American economist and strategist with \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA GETS TOUGH\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Colombia and Brazil have taken much more aggressive measures to slow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' rallies.\par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jose Dario Uribe said on Friday that the bank is not ruling out the possibility of "big" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. [ID:nN05292894]\par \par \uc2 The Andean country has already extended dollar purchases in the market but some fear the country may resort to capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real struggled on Friday, but largely because of the dollar's recovery rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had plummeted on Thursday following the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision to pump $600 billion into the economy, boosting Brazil's real to a two-week high and giving Chile's peso its biggest one-day gain in more than a year.\par \par \uc2 On Brazil's local spot market, the bid quote for the real <BRBY> traded flat for most of Friday, closing 0.12 percent weaker at 1.678 against the dollar. The U.S. data had less direct impact on Brazil, which counts China as its top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still firmed 1.37 percent over the week thanks to the post-Fed boost, its biggest weekly gain in five weeks.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101108e6b5001f3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
