\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  seesaw on Fed,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2010\par 16:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Uncertainty grows over scale of U.S. stimulus package\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real adds 0.1 pct, Mexican peso loses 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso weakens 0.6 pct, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed\par \par \uc2 * Argentina's risk spread narrows after Kirchner's death\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seesawed on Wednesday on uncertainty over the extent of likely stimulus measures to revive the U.S. economy, which are expected to boost the region's bond market.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve is expected next week to unveil a program of U.S. Treasury bond purchases worth a few hundred billion dollars over several months, the Wall Street Journal reported on Wednesday. That rattled some investors who had envisioned a bigger and more immediate stimulus package.\par \par \uc2 Such measures are likely to keep U.S. yields low, encouraging more investors to pump cash into Latin America's higher-yielding bonds.\par \par \uc2 Brazil is a prime target because its benchmark interest rate of 10.75 percent is one of the highest in the world.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> opened weaker but was later bid 0.12 percent stronger at 1.702 reais per U.S. dollar on the local spot market.\par \par \uc2 "There is some uncertainty over the Fed's policy next week so the market is 'on the fence' today," said Carlos Gandolfo, a partner at Sao Paulo's Pioneer brokerage.\par \par \uc2 But traders were also looking to get back into the market after recent losses. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has underperformed the region over the past few days because of tough action by the government to curb the real's recent rally, which is hurting exporters and widening the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently stepped up its dollar purchases in the spot market. The government also this month tripled its tax on foreign bond purchases to 6 percent and raised a tax on the collateral investors must put down to trade in the futures market. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kuv79p}}}\par \par \uc2 Analysis on Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform: [ID:nN26120199] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 But such measures may only have a short-term effect on the real, some analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Higher commodity prices and stimulus measures abroad are likely to overshadow \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , causing the real to keep appreciating, analysts at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 "Our skepticism regarding the impacts of those measures on medium- and long-term horizons led us to reduce our year-end 2010 and 2011 USD/BRL forecasts to 1.65 (from 1.72) and to 1.70 (from 1.80), respectively," they said.\par \par \uc2 EXPORTERS IN FOCUS\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> weakened 0.51 percent to 12.468 per dollar after trading at multi-month highs earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The peso has rallied about 6 percent since the end of August. But Mexico is not losing export competitiveness because of these \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, the finance minister said on Wednesday. [ID:nN27223162]\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=> weakened 0.58 percent to 494.10 per dollar, hitting its weakest level in about a month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under pressure from the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Unlike \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chile has faced growing pressure from its exporters to take action.\par \par \uc2 President Sebastian Pinera said on Monday his government is working to open capital accounts and relax limits on investments abroad to battle the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally.\par \par \uc2 Traders are concerned that more aggressive measures are on their way, such as a return to dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, the risk spread on Argentina's bonds narrowed to 511 basis points following the death of former President Nestor Kirchner. [ID:nN27249576]\par \par \uc2 The policies of Kirchner, who was expected to run for president in 2011, have caused great concern among investors. (Editing by Padraic Cassidy)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP|PCO   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101030e6ar0008y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
