\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Closes Little Changed After Breaching 12.30 Mark\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2010\par 22:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso closed little changed against the U.S. dollar Monday in a volatile session in which the rate dipped briefly below the key 12.30 level.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN12.3505, compared with MXN12.3490 at the close Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave back early gains, which were prompted by a weekend agreement by Group of 20 developed and developing nations to avoid competitive devaluations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , encouraging investors to move into emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The concern for a number of Latin American countries, and particularly Brazil, has been the appreciation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as portfolio investors pour money into their markets seeking more attractive yields.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has appreciated less than most of its regional peers, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen among the least likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly or impose capital controls.\par \par \uc2 "We do not expect the MXN to join the '\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars,'" \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  Banamex said in a report. Given the three usual options in the face of strong inflows--to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, or slash local interest rates--"we think the first option is the most likely in the case of Mexico," Banamex added.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Mexico buys up to $600 million a month under put options that can be exercised by banks when the peso is stronger than its 20-day average. On the rates front, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has held the benchmark overnight rate at 4.5% since July 2009 and is expected to leave it unchanged until the third quarter of 2011.\par \par \uc2 The recent gains in the peso, Banamex said, are probably a response to an attractive carry trade, where investors sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with low interest and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  offering higher yields.\par \par \uc2 The brief move below 12.30, and prospects of continued dollar weakness, prompted \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  to again move the target on its long peso recomendation to 12 to the dollar from 12.30, and to tighten the stop loss to 12.45 from 12.55.\par \par \uc2 ING Mexico said in a report that markets are likely to continue responding to increased appetite for risk with a weak dollar as a counterpart, and to uncertainty over how the U.S. Federal Reserve will go about quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 "The external context remains favorable for local assets and we anticipate further appreciation of the peso toward our target of 12.25," ING said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's stocks rose modestly Monday, but enough for another record-high close, while government bonds gained ground, pushing yields down. The yield on benchmark 10-year bonds fell two basis points to 6.11%, and the yield on 20-year bonds slipped one basis point to 6.81%.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980-5176, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com [ 25-10-10 2051GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101025e6ap001g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
