\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real suffers from gov't pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2010\par 15:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns push Brazil's real down 1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso adds 0.1 pct, U.S. jobs data helps\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso dips 0.1 pct after new gov't measure\par \par \uc2 By Samantha Pearson and Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 21 (Reuters) - Brazil's real underperformed the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday as moves by the government to curb the real's recent rally unsettled investors.\par \par \uc2 Late on Wednesday the country's authorities closed some loopholes in one of their most recent measures: a tax on the money investors have to put up to trade Brazilian derivatives.\par \par \uc2 The authorities blocked local banks from lending, swapping, or renting out securities to foreigners for use as collateral. It also forbid the exchange from accepting letters of credit as collateral. Shares of Brazil's BM&FBovespa exchange operator led declines on the country's stock market on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The persistent change to the rules of the game generates unwelcome uncertainty, giving the message that foreigners are not welcome in the domestic fixed-income market," wrote analysts at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazil has taken aggressive action to curb the recent rally in the real, which is making exporters' goods more expensive abroad and worsening the current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> fell 1 percent to 1.690 on the local market in intraday trading on Thursday, recoiling further from the 2-year high it hit earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 The real's losses were largely due to these new minor rule changes, said Rodrigo Nassar, head of trading at brokerage Hencorp Commcor in Sao Paulo. "This has ended up making the market uncomfortable" and is "causing more discontent," he said.\par \par \uc2 Growing expectations the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will launch a new round of asset buying, known as quantitative easing, to kick-start the economy have boosted Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to multi-month highs.\par \par \uc2 Such easing is likely to keep yields on U.S. Treasuries close to record lows, encouraging investors to flock to higher-yielding debt in Latin America.\par \par \uc2 CHILE'S PESO GETS FIRST TASTE OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  MEASURES\par \par \uc2 Chile announced on Thursday it would cut red tape on customs to help exporters hit by a strong peso as one measure to ease the effects of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid appreciation. The government also threatened that other tools could be on their way. [ID:nN21292275]\par \par \uc2 But the measure was relatively mild compared to the activities of other countries in the region and the Chilean peso <CLP=> only lost 0.05 percent to 484.65 per dollar. In the last couple of weeks, analysts have started to talk more about the possibility of government measures to tame the peso, which is trading around a 29-month high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Other potential announcements could include changes to pension fund regulations, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 As an openly traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso does not present the same \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk for investors.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the country's close trade links with the United States has been the main concern, causing volatility in the market as the outlook for the U.S. economy constantly changes.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <MXN=> crept up 0.06 percent to 12.3878 per dollar on Thursday after data showed U.S. claims for unemployment benefits fell more than expected last week, pointing to some improvement in the labor market. [ID:nN20229912] (Additional reporting by Caroline Stauffer in Mexico City; Editing by Andrea Ricci)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101024e6al00089\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
