\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico peso firms, bond yields fall to 1-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2010\par 17:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Peso firms 0.4 pct, helped by central banker's comments\par \par \uc2 * 10-year bond yields hit lowest since early May 2009\par \par \uc2 * IPC stock index falls 0.88 pct as \uc2 America Movil\uc2  drags (Adds closing stock prices, background on peso strength)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, April 21 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso firmed on Wednesday after comments from the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief cooled speculation that policymakers could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent surge.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also supported by flows into local peso bonds as investors bet Mexico's economic prospects were better than those of some countries in Europe, driving yields down to their lowest in almost a year.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> <MEX01> strengthened 0.4 percent to 12.1682 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The IPC stock index <.MXX> closed down 0.88 percent to 33,517.18, hurt by a 1.34 percent loss in shares of index heavyweight wireless provider \uc2 America Movil\uc2  .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Agustin Carstens said a recent surge in the peso's value was not excessive, according to a newspaper interview. For details see [ID:nN21183915].\par \par \uc2 "This undermines the idea that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a more aggressive way," said Daniela Blancas, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Some market players have been speculating that the peso's more than 7 percent gain this year has been making policymakers uncomfortable. A strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes exports more expensive and may crimp Mexico's rebound from a deep recession in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise the amount of dollars it buys from the market each month through a program of dollar option sales it implemented to build up reserves.\par \par \uc2 But others have speculated the bank could take even more aggressive measures such as the daily dollar auctions seen in Brazil and Colombia.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said option holders had sold $5 million to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the last of $600 million in options sold at the end of last month.\par \par \uc2 The option program has helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lift reserves to a record 97.4 billion as of the end of last week.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the government's benchmark 10-year peso bond <MX10YT=RR> bid down 10 basis points to 7.45 percent, its lowest since May 7, 2009, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Spreads between Greek and German bond yields hit a 12-year high on Wednesday, highlighting uncertainty about how Athens would resolve its debt crisis and boosting the appeal of Latin American countries with comparatively better debt profiles.\par \par \uc2 "There is a greater stability in terms of managing debt in the region of Latin America," said Alejandro Martinez, a debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The stronger peso has also helped reduce inflationary pressures by cheapening imports and analysts have been paring back expectations on when Mexico will hike interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Brokerage IXE this week said policymakers will wait until early next year before tightening borrowing costs.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will report early April consumer prices on Thursday, and analysts poll by Reuters expect a 0.12 percent rise. [ID:nN21125799]\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MEXICO/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100421e64l0016c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
