\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Foreign Reserves Up $3.86B To $90.93B As Of Dec 24\b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2009\par 16:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Mexico said Tuesday that Mexico's foreign reserves rose to $90.93 billion in the week ending Dec. 24.\par \par \uc2 Foreign reserves increased by $3.86 billion last week compared to the week ending Dec. 18 largely thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the federal government for $4.03 billion.\par \par \uc2 Outflows last week included $250 million spent by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Foreign reserves rebounded in the fourth quarter after hitting a low for the year of $72.6 billion in August as a result of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize the peso.\par \par \uc2 Foreign reserves as of Dec. 24 were $5.49 billion higher than the $85.44 billion reported at the end of 2008.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 52-55-5980-5177; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 29-12-09 1542GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091229e5ct000n1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw202\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3030\pichgoal600
