\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Gains Ground Vs Dollar; Strongest Since Jan\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 21:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso gained against the U.S. dollar for a fifth straight session Tuesday, closing at its strongest level since January as U.S. stocks surged on continued optimism about the financial sector.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN14.0450 to the dollar, compared with MXN14.5150 at the close last Friday. Local markets were closed Monday for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 Joel Virgen, an analyst at \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 . (C) unit Banamex, said the peso's recent bounce-back from record lows just over a week ago came amid a broad recovery in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with greater volatility because of Mexico's close ties to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 "Just as the peso did especially badly, this time it did especially well," he said.\par \par \uc2 The peso had sunk to an all-time low MXN15.60 to the dollar in after-hours trading March 9.\par \par \uc2 Banamex said the peso's rebound was helped by changes in the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and news that local pension fund managers will invest only in local assets for a year to help the economy.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate dipped briefly below MXN14 during Tuesday's session, as it had Monday in foreign trading with local participants absent.\par \par \uc2 The current exchange rate is "closer to levels that could be considered justified by fundamentals," Virgen said.\par \par \uc2 Solid gains in U.S. stocks, with the Dow Jones Industrial Average rising 2.5%, also contributed to the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Mexico began last week auctioning $100 million a day at market rates, and $300 million at a minimum exchange rate 2% above the previous session's "fix." Before that, the bank was auctioning $400 million at the minimum rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the $100 million Tuesday at an average MXN14.1055 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5001 5727, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com [ 17-03-09 2041GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090317e53h000qs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
