\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Mexico plays defense as economy,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  slip\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jason Lange   \par \uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 17:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 13 (Reuters) - Pummeled by a plunging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and shrinking economy, Mexican authorities are reacting with the caution of an outmatched boxer who can't land a solid punch and can only try to avoid a severe beating.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's economy is one of the most tightly linked in the world to the United States, where a deep recession is choking off demand for Mexican exports.\par \par \uc2 Analysts think Mexican output will contract about 2 percent this year, and hundreds of thousands of Mexicans have lost their jobs in recent months. Unemployment spiked to 5.0 percent in January, the highest level since 1996.\par \par \uc2 The weak economy and a retreat by Wall Street investors from emerging markets have pushed the peso to record lows against the dollar despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to prop it up by selling $20 billion from dollar reserves.\par \par \uc2 Even Mexico's president, Felipe Calderon, acknowledges that his government simply lacks the firepower to compensate for America's economic freefall -- where Mexico ships about 80 percent of its exports.\par \par \uc2 "We're too close to the earthquake's epicenter," Calderon told a conference on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Mexico became an export powerhouse after it entered the North American Free Trade Agreement, or NAFTA, with the United States and Canada in 1994. Exports are now collapsing, and fell 32 percent in January from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Calderon is running up a modest budget deficit this year to stimulate the economy but the Finance Ministry says it does not plan to ask for more deficit spending beyond what Congress authorized in October, which is equivalent to 1.8 percent of gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 Further complicating matters, the peso's rapid devaluation -- down by about a third since August -- is fueling inflation by making imports more expensive.\par \par \uc2 High inflation, in turn, has led the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take some of the punch out of its own efforts to boost the economy.\par \par \uc2 After slashing its benchmark overnight rate by 50 basis points in January, the bank cut the rate by just 25 basis points in February after data showed the peso's losses were helping to keep inflation near a seven-year high.\par \par \uc2 And while authorities stepped up efforts this week to boost the peso, they have signaled they will put tight limits on how much they will dip into the country's $80 billion in dollar reserves.\par \par \uc2 Put together, the different policy responses are seen more as a series of defensive parries than an all-out counterattack.\par \par \uc2 "They're trying not to get knocked flat," said economist Enrique Alvarez at IDEAglobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 GHOSTS OF CRISES PAST\par \par \uc2 Mexico's caution stands in contrast to Chile's more aggressive interest rate cuts and Russia's more forceful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is loathe to abandon its hard-earned principles of budgetary restraint, a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a commitment to low inflation -- all adopted in the wake of the mid-1990s financial meltdown known as the Tequila Crisis.\par \par \uc2 Going too far with fiscal, monetary or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies could make things worse, analysts say, stirring memories of the 6.2 percent economic contraction of 1995.\par \par \uc2 So policymakers have told markets they won't go to war for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2009, saying last week that Mexico will only sell the dollars it expects to accrue from 2009's oil exports -- about $19 billion over the whole year.\par \par \uc2 If authorities were to challenge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders by setting a limit on the peso's losses, as they did in the early 1990s, the risk is that they could quickly run out of dollars, triggering a collapse in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If the market goes against you they're going to try to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Flavia Cattan-Naslausky at RBS in Greenwich, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 The bank this week began selling $100 million daily into exchange markets, though that is just a fraction of the $3 billion to $5 billion in daily peso trading volumes, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> <MEX01> rose 1 percent on Friday to 14.59 per dollar, helped by growing confidence in the recovery of the U.S. banking system. The peso has posted gains this week, helped by rebounding global equities and the dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Agustin Carstens last week compared the U.S. recession to a tsunami crashing into Mexico. Nevertheless, Carstens has no plans of asking Congress to increase this year's planned budget deficit, said ministry spokesman Rodrigo Brand.\par \par \uc2 Mexico has run high deficits in the past, but a pile of debt can make lenders charge higher interest rates for both the government and private borrowers, putting the government in a precarious position and hurting the wider economy.\par \par \uc2 "You could boost spending right now, but you have to be careful that the financing of that debt is sustainable over time," said Brand.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the Finance Ministry will focus on pushing reforms for key sectors like telecommunications to improve the economy's long-term growth potential, Brand said. (Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-ECONOMY/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090316e53d001qf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
