\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico peso, stocks fall on GM bankruptcy warning\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 14:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst quote, updates with closing prices)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Reuters) - Mexico's peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened sharply and stocks fell Thursday as worries about the U.S. economy grew after auditors warned \uc2 General Motors\uc2  could face bankruptcy, a situation that could pose huge risks for Mexico's export-dependent industries.\par \par \uc2 The peso lost 0.94 percent to trade at 15.3450 per dollar as of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1:30 p.m. reference, despite news the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to buy a $100 million worth of pesos per day.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark IPC index fell 2.58 percent to close at 17,365.02 points as most major shares lost ground.\par \par \uc2 GM's auditors said Thursday there was "substantial doubt" the company could continue operating amid continued huge losses. A bankruptcy of the giant automaker would have huge repercussions for the U.S. economy and would hit Mexico's export-dependent industries hard. Mexico sends about 80 percent of its exports to the United States.\par \par \uc2 GM also operates four assembly plants and a regional engineering center in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Shares in cement maker \uc2 Cemex\uc2 , a top supplier of the U.S. construction industry, plunged 15.44 percent to 7.01 pesos. Dominant cell phone operator \uc2 America Movil\uc2  fell 2.37 percent to 18.91 pesos.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will begin daily auctions of $100 million on Monday aimed at boosting liquidity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The auction mechanism in place since October will also continue to be used, offering dollars in daily auctions at 2 percent below the rate they fetched the previous day. The amount offered daily will be reduced to $300 million from $400 million.\par \par \uc2 "We are sceptical the Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach will be very successful," RBC said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Mexico's benchmark 10-year government bond was down two basis points to 8.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 Fixed income investors are waiting for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next monthly inflation report Monday before taking large new positions, analysts said. (Reporting by Jason Lange and Robert Campbell; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MEXICO/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090305e5350016r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
