\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso slides further after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2009\par 16:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds closing prices)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Feb 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday to defend the battered peso, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to decline amid deepening worries about the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The peso sank and stocks were battered to an 18-month low by worries about the fate of top U.S. banks and after surprisingly grim U.S. economic data.\par \par \uc2 The IPC stock index <.MXX> closed down 1.63 percent at 17,752.18, its lowest close since Oct. 27.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=><MEX01> sank to 15.25 per dollar in late afternoon trade, its weakest level since new pesos were issued in 1993 after years of high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waded into the fray, selling dollars directly to brokers in a policy begun this month that marked its first direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than a decade.\par \par \uc2 That helped the peso pare loses somewhat to 15.099 per dollar, a 1.12 percent loss from Thursday, by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1:30 p.m. (1930 GMT) final reference rate.\par \par \uc2 U.S. government data on Friday showed the recession in the United States worsened in the fourth quarter even more than initially estimated, with the economy suffering its deepest contraction since early 1982.\par \par \uc2 That bodes ill for Mexico, which sends around 80 percent of its exports to its northern neighbor.\par \par \uc2 "There will be a similar drop during the first quarter, reflecting the deterioration of dollar flows to this country," including tourism and exports," said Mario Copca, an analyst at MetAnalisis consultancy in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Also weighing was news that the U.S. government is boosting its equity stake in \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2  , which raised worries about which other U.S. banks might see similar actions.\par \par \uc2 The news stirred speculation that Mexican investors could end up buying Citi's local unit, Banamex. For details, see [ID:nN27355348]\par \par \uc2 But analysts said that in the case of any such sale, the Mexican government could help arrange financing and mitigate the impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has lost more than a third of its value against the dollar since August.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold around $18.5 billion to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since October though dollar auctions and the direct sales this month.\par \par \uc2 In stock trading, financial group Inbursa <GFINBURO.MX> shed 6.97 percent to 29.11 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Soriana <SORIANAB.MX>, Mexico's No. 2 retailer by sales, plunged 12.65 percent to 19.96 pesos after reporting that its fourth-quarter net profit sank 72 percent. [ID:nN27461528] (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MEXICO/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090227e52r001i5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
