\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Bets rise on Mexico debt downgrade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Noel Randewich   \par \uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2009\par 18:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Reuters) - Traders in Mexican debt are increasingly betting the country may be downgraded by credit ratings agencies, worsening already tight financing conditions as the economy stumbles into a recession.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring Mexico's sovereign debt against default has surged by a third this month and is now more expensive than insuring Brazilian bonds -- which enjoy a lower credit rating.\par \par \uc2 A slumping economy as well as falling oil exports, which fund a third of Mexico's government spending, are making the country's investment-grade debt less attractive to investors as they look toward future government budgets.\par \par \uc2 "People are expressing a negative view when it comes to Mexico. There are a lot of challenges and headwinds Mexico has to face right now," said Nick Chamie, global head of emerging market research at RBC in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 Even a war between rival drug gangs that killed 6,000 people last year is seen as weighing against Mexico.\par \par \uc2 In November, credit rating agency Fitch Ratings revised its sovereign credit rating outlooks for Mexico to negative from stable, warning about the deepening U.S. recession, tight liquidity in financial markets and falling crude prices.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's economy is expected to shrink more than 1.0 percent this year as U.S. demand for the country's manufactured exports dries up.\par \par \uc2 Mexican oil production fell 9.2 percent in January to its lowest level since November 1995 as output from the aging Cantarell oil field dwindled.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are skeptical that state oil company \uc2 Pemex\uc2  can reach production targets this year.\par \par \uc2 "The recession, political risk -- it's more than oil, but I think oil is an important part of the story," said Alonso Cervera, an economist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 LINE IN THE SAND\par \par \uc2 Raising concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserve stockpile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market to buy pesos this month after a mechanism of regular auctions established in October failed to stem losses in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Experts have questioned how far the bank might be willing to go to defend the peso, hurt by global risk aversion and the economic downturn, and whether its war chest of $82 billion in foreign reserves is enough to fight a prolonged campaign.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring $10 million of Mexico's five-year dollar bonds for a year Wednesday was $452,000, higher than investors were paying to insure similar Brazilian debt, according to Markit data service. At the end of last year, it was slightly cheaper to ensure Mexican debt than Brazilian.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that the price has gone up tells you about the perception of eventual default risk, but the levels we're talking about are still quite low," said Cervera.\par \par \uc2 Lower ratings on Mexican debt, even if still within the investment-grade range, would likely make it more expensive for the government to issue bonds.\par \par \uc2 A sharp rise in violence as Mexican soldiers battle drug cartels is also weighing on sentiment for Mexican assets.\par \par \uc2 "There is an increasing awareness of public security issues in Mexico. That is certainly being picked up in some circles and is being added to the list of reasons to sell Mexico," Chamie said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico is rated "BBB+" by both \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  and Fitch Ratings and "Baa1" by Moody's Investors Service. All of the ratings are three notches above the minimum investment grade credit rating.\par \par \uc2 Fitch and \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  rate Brazil's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt at "BBB-" but Moody's Investors Service still rates Brazil's sovereign bonds below investment grade.\par \par \uc2 ROOM TO RUN\par \par \uc2 Mexico has hedged its oil exports this year at $70 a barrel, in line with its budget and far higher than current prices of around $36 for the country's blend of crude.\par \par \uc2 But ongoing low oil prices and production could force the government to cut spending or accept a deficit in its 2010 budget.\par \par \uc2 A decade of conservative fiscal policy have given President Felipe Calderon room to run a small deficit for 2009 to boost spending on infrastructure investment as well as health and education as part of its plan to bolster the economy.\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  estimated in a report that a continued weak exchange rate could help boost revenues in pesos from oil sales next year, helping limit the government's revenue shortfall to around 1.0 percent. (Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-DEBT/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090228e52p000lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
