\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico Peso Rebounds On Equity Gains After Record Low\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2009\par 22:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso strengthened Tuesday after closing at a record low versus the dollar in the previous session, as large gains in local stocks and higher oil prices supported a relief rally.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted in Mexico City closing at MXN14.8255 to the dollar, compared with MXN14.8620 in morning trading and MXN14.95 at Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 Ramses Villela, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Bulltick Capital Markets in Mexico City, said the gains will probably be short-lived.\par \par \uc2 "In technical terms, we're still in a bull market," Villela said, adding the peso would have to strengthen to MXN14.35 to mark a change in tendency and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still pushing to break the MXN15 level.\par \par \uc2 Opinions among analysts vary as to whether the peso's recent depreciation - to its current value from MXN10 to the dollar a little more than six months ago - is based on Mexico's economic fundamentals or the broader market's aversion to risk and shortage of liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it sold $155 million through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market last week, in addition to the $1.06 billion it sold earlier this month, to curtail the peso's recent volatility.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Finance Ministry deny having a target for the exchange rate, concerns are growing that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness may be feeding local inflation in addition to weighing on the balance sheets of local companies with dollar-denominated debt.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Mexico reported Tuesday the country's inflation was higher than anticipated in the first half of February, with the consumer price index rising 0.17%, compared with economists' expectations of 0.14%.\par \par \uc2 Core inflation, which excludes the cost of energy and fresh produce, rose 0.29% in the first two weeks of the month, above the market's forecast of a 0.22% rise. The annual core inflation rate increased to 5.81% from 5.76% at the end of January.\par \par \uc2 "Merchandise goods other than processed foods are clearly suffering from the pass-through of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  economist Rafael de la Fuente said in a note.\par \par \uc2 -By Paul Kiernan, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255)5001-5726; paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 24-02-09 2112GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090224e52o000w8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
