\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Mkt Debt Slumps As Morning Gains Lost To Gloom\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2009\par 22:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market bonds slumped Monday as early morning risk tolerance gave way to far darker thoughts on the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Risk premiums, as measured by \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's Emerging Markets Bond Index Global, were five basis points wider on the day, at 690 basis points over U.S. Treasurys, with returns -0.26%.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Brazil 2040 Global was bid 3/4 lower at 122 7/16, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  gave Venezuela a boost by nudging its recommendation on the country's debt back to neutral from underweight.\par \par \uc2 "In the aftermath of President Chavez's victory in last Sunday's referendum, the coast is now much clearer politically for the government to make a long-overdue macroeconomic adjustment to address the reality of lower oil prices," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Despite ongoing fundamental deterioration, the market pricing of Venezuela at near-default levels is exaggerated, it said. "Investors seem to agree with this view, as the reduction of Venezuela underweights was one of the most salient trends of our February client survey," it said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market Monday as the peso approached a record low close against the dollar and neared the psychological barrier of MXN15.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in Mexico said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in late in the session to sell an unspecified amount of dollars directly to trading desks.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate immediately fell from around MXN14.93 to the dollar to MXN14.83, one trader said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's spread on EMBIG was two basis points tighter, at 431 basis points over Treasurys, while the 2034 Global was bid 3/8 lower at 91 5/8, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Latin American countries in general saw their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady against the U.S. dollar in New York trading Monday, while Eastern Europe and Asia saw some gains versus the greenback. The Croatian kune in particular was stronger at HRK5.79, from Friday's close of HRK5.90.\par \par \uc2 Chile's Finance Ministry will transfer $3 billion in assets from one of its sovereign wealth funds to finance part of its $4 billion fiscal stimulus package, the ministry said Monday. The funds will be withdrawn from the Economic and Social Stabilization Fund, which currently has about $20.21 billion in assets.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso lost slightly against the dollar, at CLP623.55 from Friday's CLP622.10. The country's spread on EMBIG was three basis points tighter at 351 basis points over Treasurys.\par \par \uc2 In the Middle East, the United Arab Emirates said it will provide $10 billion in funding to Dubai, which will help the stricken state service its heavy debt load as it copes with a tanking real-estate market and tepid appetite among international lenders to extend further credit.\par \par \uc2 In the corporate world, Fitch Ratings further downgraded the credit ratings of Mexican cement maker \uc2 Cemex\uc2  SAB (CX) Monday, citing concerns about the company's high level of debt in the ongoing economic downturn.\par \par \uc2 Fitch lowered \uc2 Cemex\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuer default rating to 'BB' from 'BB+,' and cut its national rating to 'A+(mex)' from 'AA-(mex),' affecting the ratings on a number of obligations.\par \par \uc2 The ratings agency said it expects \uc2 Cemex\uc2  to see continued pressure on earnings this year because of sharp economic downturns in the U.S., Spain and the U.K. and weakness in other markets, while the company faces challenges in its efforts to sell about $2 billion in assets.\par \par \uc2 -By Matthew Cowley, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 5692; matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 23-02-09 2159GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1179 1810 1833 4071   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090223e52n000re\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
