\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2009\par 20:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmation)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Feb 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, offering dollars directly to dealers after the peso hit a record low against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement the sales were aimed at improving liquidity in the market. The peso hit a record low earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 The bank did not say how many dollars it had sold in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which traders reported hours before the bank's announcement.\par \par \uc2 The peso rallied as the bank offered dollars after it finished its regular dollar auctions at 1 p.m. (1900 GMT).\par \par \uc2 The peso had fallen more than 2 percent and traded as low as 14.9983 per dollar <MEX01> on Friday, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the maximum $400 million in two auctions under its daily dollar auction policy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose following the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but was still down 1.22 percent at 14.80 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The bank began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Feb. 4, selling dollars directly to banks in its first such direct sale in a decade.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Agustin Carstens said on Feb. 6 that the bank would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary to contain the volatility of the peso. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle, Liz Salazar, Lorena Segura, Jason Lange and Robert Campbell; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090220e52k001qg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
