\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Mexico sold $1.06 bln last week to protect peso\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2009\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds trader's quote and background)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 10 (Reuters) - Mexico sold $1.06 billion from its foreign reserves last week in extraordinary sales to boost the sagging peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In a weekly report, the bank said total international reserves fell in the week to Feb. 6 to $82.085 billion, adding that a big part of the fall was due to the extraordinary sales.\par \par \uc2 The bank surprised the market last week by selling dollars directly to banks and brokerages, halting a slide in the peso, which has been hit by a drop in exports to the United States -- the first move of that type in more than a decade.\par \par \uc2 Until then, Mexico had been selling dollars only through auctions with predictable rules aimed at stopping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling too sharply on any given day.\par \par \uc2 Market players said the amount announced was in line with expectations.\par \par \uc2 "The amount (of dollars) sold was nothing," said a Mexico City trader.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> <MEX01> sank to 1.14 percent to 14.36 pesos per dollar on concerns about U.S. plans to save its economy and over worries Fitch might lower Mexico's credit rating.\par \par \uc2 The peso has lost about a quarter of its value against the dollar since August due to the global financial crisis and a worsening recession in Mexico's biggest trading partner, the United States.\par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings said on Monday it is carefully monitoring \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the magnitude of the country's economic contraction, and the impact of the downturn on its fiscal and current accounts to decide on whether to downgrade its debt ratings.\par \par \uc2 International reserves finished the week ending Jan. 30 at $83.631 billion. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned $400 million on Feb 3 at its regular auctions. (Reporting by Jason Lange and Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090210e52a001vt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
