\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso holds  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  gains; bonds slip\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2009\par 15:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds closing stock prices)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Feb 9 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on Monday as investors expected the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep up with last week's landmark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> firmed 0.09 percent to 14.197 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars directly to banks last week for the first time in a decade, which helped pull the peso back from a record low hit last Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 While the bank did not enter into direct sales on Monday, Finance Minister Agustin Carstens last week said it would continue to defend the battered peso.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also uncertain about the success of plans in Washington to shore up American banks and a congressional vote on a stimulus package to boost the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has lost around a quarter of its value since last August as investors dumped emerging market assets and Mexico's economy slowed due to falling demand in its chief export market, the United States.\par \par \uc2 "If the U.S. economy doesn't turn around so that it helps our economy it will be very difficult for these \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop capital from flowing out," said Juan Carlos Lopez, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at brokerage Intercam in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the market will be monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserve level, which will be posted on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Evidence of a big sell-off in reserves could alarm investors, said Gabriel Casillas, an economist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The bank has spent nearly $17 billion since October in regular dollar auctions to support the peso, but last week it became more aggressive.\par \par \uc2 Carstens suggested that traders had been gaming the predictability of the dollar auctions for profit.\par \par \uc2 Mexican bonds slipped as some investors pared bets on how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lower borrowing costs this month.\par \par \uc2 The government's benchmark 10-year peso bond <MX10YT=RR> fell 0.562 of a point in price, pushing its yield up to 8.06 percent.\par \par \uc2 A report on Monday showed annual inflation slowed in January, possibly giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more room to lower interest rates. For more see [ID:nN09367278].\par \par \uc2 In the equities market, the IPC stock index <.MXX> closed up 0.48 percent at 20,537.10 points, led by a 1.61 percent gain in shares of top retailer \uc2 Wal-Mart de Mexico\uc2  <WALMEXV.MX> ahead of its earnings report later this week.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Walmex, as the company is known, rose 0.48 centavos to 30.31 pesos. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MEXICO/ (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090209e529001j2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
