\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  to keep  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market -finmin\b0\par\par\uc2 By Walter Brandimarte and Herbert Lash   \par \uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2009\par 15:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds quote from Carstens, background)\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Feb 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a bid to stabilize the peso, will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with dollar auctions and a surprising new policy of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to banks, Finance Minister Agustin Carstens said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars directly to banks since Wednesday to stop certain market participants from "destabilizing the market," Carstens said.\par \par \uc2 He said some investors were trying to utilize the predictability of the dollar auction mechanism to generate profits.\par \par \uc2 "Therefore, to try to basically guarantee a more orderly working of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, that's why the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  committee decided to slightly modify its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told investors at a Mexican housing conference in New York.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised investors on Wednesday by selling dollars directly to banks for the first time in more than 10 years as fears the U.S. downturn is driving Mexico into recession sent the peso tumbling to its weakest level since 1993, when "new" pesos were introduced.\par \par \uc2 The peso has weakened about 25 percent against the dollar since mid-September, when emerging markets were engulfed by a credit crisis that sharply widened following the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Carstens said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to auction $400 million when the dollar appreciates more than 2 percent against the peso on a single session. But it will "reserve the right" to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary.\par \par \uc2 He said that, unlike a decade ago, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently not the epicenter of a global financial crisis. He said the recent strength of the dollar is "strange" because the United States is the center of the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Mexico spun into a deep recession in the 1990s after a sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation triggered financial upheaval in the country and across Latin America in what was called the "Tequila crisis."\par \par \uc2 The Mexican government will do everything in its means to support the economy, Carstens said, including increasing public expenditures and further loosening monetary policy. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates by 50 basis points last month.\par \par \uc2 "We expect that in the coming months we will see more of this," the minister said.\par \par \uc2 He also said Mexico is in a position of strength with a healthy financial system, solid public finances and a far better sovereign debt profile than in the past. (Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CARSTENS/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|MNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090206e526001yk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
