\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Ends Stronger At 14.1970/Dlr On Ctrl Bank Move\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2009\par 21:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso gained against the U.S. dollar for a third straight day Friday, thanks to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unhappy with recent pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN14.1970 to the dollar, stronger than its MXN14.2830 close on Thursday but weaker from an earlier level of MXN14.15. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains down 2.7% year-to-date after a 21% depreciation in 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Mexico stepped into the market Wednesday as the peso reached an all-time low MXN14.70, selling dollars directly to banks and without disclosing the amounts being sold.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which continued Thursday and Friday, were seen as a way of discouraging bets against the peso.\par \par \uc2 The exchange commission, formed by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Finance Ministry officials, confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said the amounts will be reflected in weekly reports on foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Agustin Carstens said in New York Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were necessary as some market participants were seeking to make profits on the weaker peso, and authorities will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever necessary to maintain an orderly market.\par \par \uc2 The direct sales are in addition to the $400 million the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions each day at a minimum exchange rate 2% above the previous session, and estimates have varied on how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have sold.\par \par \uc2 The Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  described it as a "tricky strategy."\par \par \uc2 While relatively small amounts could discourage speculation by introducing two-way risk in the market, if the recent depreciation is the result of rising risk aversion, "the risk is that Banxico will need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively to hold the peso," RBS said in a report Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  unit Banamex said the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly suggests authorities took the view that the weakening was market-driven.\par \par \uc2 In a report, Banamex rejected as a justification for the recent extent of the depreciation the notion that Mexico's external accounts will suffer if the economy follows the U.S. into recession.\par \par \uc2 "Mexican exports are undoubtedly affected by weaker U.S. demand. However, due to the nature of the North American economic integration, Mexican exports are import-intensive," Banamex said.\par \par \uc2 The bank noted a 91% correlation between imports and exports since Nafta went into effect in 1994, compared with 40% in the previous decade-and-a-half.\par \par \uc2 "In terms of the peso scenario, that means that the argument that associates a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a wider trade deficit should be clarified," Banamex said.\par \par \uc2 Banamex said it sees no problem with Mexico meeting its 2009 financing needs and said the widening of spreads on the country's credit default swaps to 386 basis points from 292 basis points at the end of 2008 wasn't justified by fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  attributed the peso weakening largely to a rapid deterioration in the macroeconomic outlook.\par \par \uc2 "Technicals and financial variables only partially explain observed depreciation year-to-date, suggesting largely fundamentals-driven price action," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said in a mid-week report.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Mexico, meanwhile, is considered to have abundant ammunition to maintain a defense of the peso. In additional to $84 billion in foreign reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week extended to Oct. 30 its $30 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap facility with the U.S. Federal Reserve, which gives it another channel of access to dollars.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5001 5727, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Claudia Assis in New York contributed to this report) [ 06-02-09 2042GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090206e526001cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
