\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  and stocks gain, helped by US rally\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2009\par 22:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * LatAm \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Risk appetite gives stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  a boost\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  a second day to prop up peso\par \par \uc2 By Daniel Bases\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks gained ground in tandem with rising U.S. equities on Thursday as investors took an optimistic view that a U.S. accounting rule change would be implemented.\par \par \uc2 The change, a relaxation of an accounting requirement on the recognition of losses that has resulted in billions of losses for banks, is potentially part of the Obama administration's plans to shore up the shattered U.S. financial system.\par \par \uc2 While emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks rose on the better risk appetite, benchmark sovereign bonds were weaker.\par \par \uc2 Rising U.S. Treasuries however helped push spreads versus emerging market bonds one basis point narrower to 638 basis points, according to the benchmark \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus <11EMJ><.JPMEMBIPLUS>.\par \par \uc2 "There is a degree of randomness in day-to-day trading, but in general, environments where equities are improving and bonds are selling off is a world where risk appetite is normalizing and that is a good thing," said Don Hanna, head of emerging markets economics and market analysis at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's emerging markets stock index <.MSCIEF> rose 0.4 percent while the Latin American stock index <.MILA00000PUS> gained 1.94 percent.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's sovereign bond led to the downside, dropping 1.44 points in price to bid 107.688, yielding 7.108 percent <MEXGLB22=RR>.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second day in a row on Thursday to prop up the peso against the U.S. dollar, introducing unannounced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market psychology, which is catching investors off-guard.\par \par \uc2 The peso rose 0.77 percent to 14.36 per U.S. dollar <MEX01>.\par \par \uc2 "The peso is down 27 percent over the past five months, the worst performer among the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as expectations that a worsening U.S. recession will further depress Mexican exports and drive down remittances from the U.S. to Mexico, further," BullTick Capital Markets wrote clients.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets, especially Mexico, face strong negative pressures on their economic activity as a result of the U.S. recession and precarious outlook, with or without more government spending plans.\par \par \uc2 Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, Latin America strategist at RBS in Greenwich, Connecticut said there were no dominant themes in current trade on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It is a combination of factors. Stronger U.S. equities is always a help but also we are feeling the tailwind of a recent risk rally. The fact that we are breaking these technical levels also, just adds to the move," she said.\par \par \uc2 Cattan-Naslausky highlighted the Brazilian real's break below the 2.32 level as a major significant movement that is pushing it toward the 2.25 per U.S. dollar level. The real was quoted at 2.2850, up 1.18 percent against the greenback late on Thursday <BRBY>.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market credit default swaps recovered some ground after a shaky start to the North American trading session.\par \par \uc2 "From credit standpoint we are rebounding a bit from the early weakness, but I think people are not sure if it is going to hold," said one trader at a U.S. hedge fund.\par \par \uc2 "The accounting rule change that they are talking about has helped boost equities and that's spilling over into emerging," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING/|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090208e525000ky\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
