\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-LatAm stocks gain on commodities, US data\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2009\par 19:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * US service sector data triggers commodities, stocks rally\par \par \uc2 * EMBI+ spreads near two-month tight, \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  issues bond\par \par \uc2 * LatAm \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mixed on rates outlook, commodity rally\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with direct dollar sales (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Latin American stocks rose along with commodity prices on Wednesday, after better-than-expected data on the U.S. services sector supported investors' appetite for risk in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Taking advantage of the improved sentiment, Brazilian state-owned oil firm \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  tapped international capital markets to sell $1.5 billion in 10-year bonds at a yield of 8.125 pct, below the initial guidance. For details, see [ID:nN04281861].\par \par \uc2 The benchmark MSCI stock index for Latin America <.MILA00000PUS> climbed 1.82 percent as higher metal prices improved the economic outlook for some raw material exporting countries in the region.\par \par \uc2 Market sentiment improved after a report showed the U.S. service sector shrank less than expected in January, raising hopes that consumer spending is slowly recovering.\par \par \uc2 "With the positive news overseas, investors who were betting stocks would fall are now cutting their short positions," said Roberto Alem, an economist with M2 Investimentos in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The most important Latin American stock indexes were in the black, with the Brazilian Bovespa index <.BVSP> gaining 0.96 percent and the Argentine MerVal <.MERV> rising 0.62 percent.\par \par \uc2 But Mexico's IPC <.MXX> erased early gains to close practically flat after Wall Street turned red.\par \par \uc2 Rekindled appetite for risk caused yield spreads between emerging-market global bonds and U.S. Treasuries to narrow 15 basis points to a near two-month tight of 625 basis points, according to the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  EMBI+ index <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 The spreads narrowed despite the downgrade of Russia's sovereign credit ratings by Fitch earlier in the day. The decision was based on the recent fall in commodity prices, high capital outflows, falling reserves and corporate problems, the ratings agency said. For details, see [ID:nL476617].\par \par \uc2 With the issuance window open, \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 ' bond deal attracted some $4.5 billion in demand, reported IFR, a Thomson-Reuters publication. The deal was managed by Santander, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  and \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed, however. Some were supported by the rise in commodity prices and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while others were pressured by the outlook for more aggressive monetary policy easing in the region.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> gained 0.39 percent to 2.312 per U.S. dollar while the Mexican peso <MXN=> strengthened 0.76 percent to 14.47 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was further supported by an unusual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold dollars directly to banks rather than auctioning them as usual, market sources said. [ID:nN04315510]\par \par \uc2 Among the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Colombian peso <COP=RR> lost 1.14 percent to 2,473.95 per dollar as some investors believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will need to ease its monetary policy more aggressively, after cutting rates by 50 basis points to 9 percent last week. (Additional reporting by Aluisio Alves in Sao Paulo)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090207e524000e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
