\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Closes Stronger At 12.4160/Dlr; Stocks Gain\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2008\par 21:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso closed stronger Monday as demand for dollars from foreign investors eased as the local stock market rallied.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico City, the peso was quoted as closing at 12.4160 to the dollar, slightly weaker than MXN12.29 at the open but stronger than MXN13.0525 at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 One Mexico City-based trader said foreign investors have stopped selling stocks and then buying dollars, a practice that contributed to a dive in the peso last week and prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell over $8.9 billion in reserves to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The IPC stock index was trading up 9.2% at 19,905.2 points.\par \par \uc2 On Monday there were no takers at dollar auctions by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had been set up to contain recent exchange market volatility.\par \par \uc2 The bank has set up daily dollar auctions in which it offers $400 million at a rate 2% higher than the previous day's "fix." But the peso's rally Monday removed the need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The minimum price for Monday's auctions was MXN13.3484, while the peso was quoted on the market at MXN12.3990 at 2:40 p.m. EDT, when the auction took place. The minimum price for Tuesday's auctions will be MXN12.6218.\par \par \uc2 Market watchers expect the peso to continue firming.\par \par \uc2 "It's hard to forecast what levels the peso will be at in coming days, however, we think that with the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's experience in this kind of situation, the exchange rate could settle around MXN12 for several weeks before beginning to come down," the Mexican Institute of Finance Executives said in a report.\par \par \uc2 -By Peter Millard, Dow Jones Newswires; 5255-5001-5724; peter.millard@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Corrected October 13, 2008 15:50 ET (19:50 GMT) [ 13-10-08 1932GMT ]\par \par \uc2 The IPC stock index was trading up 9.2% at 19,905.2 points.\par \par \uc2 (A story published at 3:32 p.m. EDT misstated the level of the IPC stock index) [ 13-10-08 1950GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081013e4ad000vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
