\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks in relentless sell-off, bonds sink\b0\par\par\uc2 1,402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 23:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging market stocks down over 50 percent this year\par \par \uc2 * Latin American central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stocks drop\par \par \uc2 * Sovereign debt yield spreads widest in 5-1/2 years\par \par \uc2 * Investors looking to IMF meeting for answers (Updates with IMF/G7 details, closing prices, comment)\par \par \uc2 By Daniel Bases\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 10 (Reuters) - The relentless slide in global markets swept emerging market assets to fresh multi-year lows on Friday with investors succumbing to panic selling while credit markets remain frozen.\par \par \uc2 In Washington, Group of Seven finance ministers struggled to agree on a unified approach to cure the crisis that threatens to trigger a deep global recession. (For more, click on [ID:nN10398960].)\par \par \uc2 Ministers of the Group of 24 developing nations called for a comprehensive response to the crisis and said the balance of risks is shifting to slower growth as inflation recedes. (For more, click on [ID:nWBT009978].)\par \par \uc2 A handful of emerging market bourses were shut down on Friday rather than risk further declines.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President George W. Bush implored Americans to remain confident on Friday and promised to restore stability. (For more, click on [ID:nN10363000] and [ID:nG7G8].)\par \par \uc2 The MSCI emerging markets stock index fell to a three-year low, dropping 4.75 percent, or 29.40 points to 589.50. The index is down 20 percent this week and nearly 53 percent for the year <.MSCIEF>.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America the picture was similar. The MSCI Latin American stock index tumbled 7.97 percent or 173.41 points to 2001.71. The index is down nearly 29 percent this week and 54 percent for the year <.MILA00000PUS>.\par \par \uc2 "There is tremendous uncertainty about the future path of the world economy and with more and more converging consensus that we will have a synchronized global recession," said George Hoguet, portfolio manager and emerging markets investment strategist at \uc2 State Street Global Advisors\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If that is the case, commodity prices will continue to fall and earnings estimates for emerging market companies will continue to be downgraded," he said,\par \par \uc2 According to Hoguet, emerging market corporate earnings valuations are reasonable, based on forward earnings forecasts of 7.5 percent to 8.0 percent.\par \par \uc2 But there is little confidence in the accuracy of estimates "and of course, emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been weakening and the Treasury/eurodollar spreads continue to rise," he said.\par \par \uc2 On a year-to-date basis, the MSCI emerging markets index has lost $1.82 trillion in market value while the Latin American index is down $376.6 billion, according to Reuters EcoWin data.\par \par \uc2 For perspective, MSCI's main world index has suffered a $13.5 trillion loss of value -- with more than half of that since \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  declared bankruptcy on Sept. 15.\par \par \uc2 Among the major bourses in Latin America, Brazil's Bovespa index <.BVSP> was off 3.97 percent and Mexico's IPC index <.MXX> fell 1.99 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 BOND SPREADS WIDEST IN FIVE YEARS\par \par \uc2 Emerging market sovereign bonds were trounced on Friday, pushing spreads wider by 56 basis points to 602 bps over weaker U.S. Treasuries. At one point the spread widened to 610 basis points, its worst level since April 11, 2003.\par \par \uc2 Year to date, the \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  EMBI+ index is down 18.44 percent <11EMJ>. In 2007, the index returned 6.452 percent.\par \par \uc2 One illustration of the carnage in emerging market sovereign bonds is the plunge in market capitalization versus a minor drop in the face amount of bonds outstanding.\par \par \uc2 Until this wholesale sell-off of assets with even a whiff of risk, emerging market economies had held up relatively well given rising foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 At the end of last year, the market capitalization for these bonds stood at $210 billion, according \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , while the outstanding face amount was $182 billion. Year to date, the market cap has plummeted to $170 billion while the face amount stands relatively unchanged.\par \par \uc2 That means $40 billion in market value has been wiped away, as of Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Brazil's 2040 Global bond <BRAGLB40=RR> fell 4.63 points in price to bid 109, yielding 9.192 percent. At one point, the yield hit 10.168 percent, a four-year high.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's 2030 global bond <TRGLB30=RR> fell 12.94 points in price to bid 121.313, yielding 9.516 percent. In early New York trade, the bond fell 16.25 points in price, driving the yield to a better than four-year high of 9.836 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  defended the peso again on Friday with the sale of $6.4 billion on Friday, pulling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from 14.075 per dollar, the weakest point since "new pesos" were introduced in 1993.\par \par \uc2 In midday New York trade, the peso was still down 3.877 percent at 13.05 per dollar. For the year, the peso is down over 15 percent against the greenback. <MX01><MXN=>.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $8.9 billion to defend the peso this week, more than 10 percent of the $84 billion the bank reported holding as of Oct. 3.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real fell 5.3 percent <BRBY> to 2.326 per dollar on Friday. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  flooded the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with three auctions of U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold over $500 million to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 In formal trade between banks <ARS=RASL>, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso closed 0.31 percent firmer at 3.22/3.2225 per dollar. In informal trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, as measured by Reuters, the peso closed down 1.2 percent at 3.36/3.37 per U.S. dollar <ARSB=>. The peso is at its weakest level since a 2002 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell U.S. dollars in an attempt to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, from falling. The sol <PEN=PE> slid 0.6 percent to 3.105 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Late on Thursday, Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it eliminated a deposit requirement on foreign debt. (For more, click on [ID:nN09339141].)\par \par \uc2 "Some individual corporates are going through stress but as a sector, EM is not going belly up, we're not talking about a sovereign that is struggling or about extremely leveraged economies having to unwind," Drausio Giacomelli, head of emerging markets strategy at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "It does look like the EM of the past, but when you look more closely, the problems are concentrated in some smaller countries and specific markets. Systemically the regions will have to suffer through the adjustment because of the magnitude of the shock coming from the developed world has been massive. Therefore I wouldn't say we're back to a domino environment of the 1990's or early 2000's, but you may see some casualties."\par \par \uc2 Euroclear Bank, Europe's largest securities settlement firm, said on Friday it had resumed cash settlements in Icelandic crowns, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained suspended for settlement of securities transactions.\par \par \uc2 Iceland's crown <ISK=><EURISK=> plunged in value this week after the Icelandic government was forced to take over three major banks, and remains volatile on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. (For more, click on [ID:nLA616407].)\par \par \uc2 BOURSES SHUT\par \par \uc2 Russia's stock market remained shut on Friday but authorities planned to reopen on Monday. The government pledged 350 billion roubles to support stocks. (For more, click on [ID:nLA314643].)\par \par \uc2 Russia was among a handful that either didn't open or shut down after steep losses.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's PFTS bourse was also closed. President Viktor Yushchenko, who called for a snap election in December, asked for funds to organize the polls from Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko. The two could not keep their ruling coalition together. (For more, click on [ID:nLA624975].)\par \par \uc2 Peru's stock exchange indefinitely suspended trade on Friday after the IGRA index <.IGRA> plummetted over 11 percent to 7,606, its largest drop ever.\par \par \uc2 In Washington, the White House dismissed suggestions that U.S. markets would be suspended so international financial rules could be rewritten. (Additional reporting by Manuela Badawy and Dan Burns in New York; Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City; Jorge Otaola and Walter Bianchi in Buenos Aires; Jean Luis Arce in Lima)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|UKI|CANT|AUF|J|Z|ABX|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081013e4aa0020p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
