\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Stocks Down On US Drop; Peso Weakens Vs Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Harrup   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2008\par 22:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's stocks accelerated their losses and the peso weakened against the dollar Thursday as U.S. stocks entered a late-session drop amid persistent worries about the global credit situation.\par \par \uc2 The local stock market's IPC index of leading issues closed down 1.8% or 368.77 points to 20,310.20. Volume was 288.6 million shares worth 5.52 billion pesos ($420 million).\par \par \uc2 The late drop in stocks was brought on by a dive in U.S. equities, where the Dow Jones Industrials fell 7.3%.\par \par \uc2 "As long as international markets are weak, we will perform in a similar way," said a Mexico City-based equities analyst.\par \par \uc2 The peso lost ground in late trading against the dollar, and was quoted in Mexico City at MXN13.15 around 4:10 p.m. EDT.\par \par \uc2 The peso weakened following a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar auction in which it sold $1.502 billion at an average exchange rate of MXN12.0794. Demand was $6.29 billion.\par \par \uc2 The depreciation wasn't enough to trigger dollar sales at subsequent auctions for $400 million, which are offered at a minimum rate of 2% above the previous day's "fix" - or MXN13.30.\par \par \uc2 The "fix" Thursday was MXN12.4433, putting the minimum exchange rate for Friday's $400 million auction at MXN12.6922.\par \par \uc2 The daily auctions for $400 million will be conducted until further notice.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which began Wednesday, will take time to settle the market, although Thursday's session was a lot less volatile that the previous one.\par \par \uc2 Leading the decline in stocks were the CPO shares of cement giant \uc2 Cemex\uc2  (CX), which fell 15% to MXN10.52 after \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  cut the stock to "hold" from "buy," saying it should have done so four months ago. Homebuilder \uc2 Homex\uc2  (HXM) shares fell 10% to MXN43.37.\par \par \uc2 At the close, \uc2 Cemex\uc2  joined other companies that have issued statements on their financial conditions, given recent investor jitters over credit. \uc2 Cemex\uc2  said recent market volatility has led to a negative $500 million mark-to-market value in its derivatives position, compared with a positive $100 million at the end of September.\par \par \uc2 "We continue to have cash on hand to meet all of our \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial requirements," \uc2 Cemex\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 IPC heavyweight \uc2 America Movil\uc2  (AMX) L shares held out for a 1.7% gain to MXN21.20, and debt-free retailer \uc2 Wal-Mart de Mexico\uc2  (WMMVY) V shares rose 1.2% to MXN31.01.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds were steadier than stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yield on 10-year bonds was flat at 8.54%, and the yield on 20-year bonds rose 3 basis points to 8.7%.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market after the peso weakened beyond MXN14 to the dollar Wednesday, its lowest ever level, causing the market to seize up.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered $2.5 billion but placed only $998 million, with the rest sold Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 Analysts widely praised the decision by the exchange commission, which includes \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry officials, to dip into the country's $84 billion foreign reserves to shore up the peso.\par \par \uc2 "We're convinced that fundamental variables don't concur with the depreciation of the peso," \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  (C) unit Banamex said in a report.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5001 5727, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     (Peter Millard contributed to this article) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-10-08 2054GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1027 1852 5047   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081009e4a9001ak\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
