\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso hit by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters; stocks up\b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2008\par 15:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Aug 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened on Wednesday, hit by worries the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may act to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bets that a series of interest rate hikes may be nearly over, while stocks jumped on a drop in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The peso <MXN=> <MEX01> weakened 0.25 percent to 9.9295 per dollar while the IPC stock index <.MXX> closed 1.30 percent higher at 27,342.39 points.\par \par \uc2 It was the second straight day of losses for the peso on speculation Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may begin as soon as this week to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, possibly by selling pesos.\par \par \uc2 "This was a speculative movement and the market is understanding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be hitting an important floor," said Mario Copca, an analyst at MetAnalisis consultancy in Mexico City.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Guillermo Ortiz last week said an exaggerated strengthening of the peso would be inconvenient, leading some market players to bet on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso gained more than 4 percent against the dollar between June and the beginning of August as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key interest rate to 8 percent, attracting foreign investors looking to beat paltry yields on U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 While many analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike interest rates again at its meeting this month to fight rising inflation, some investors are betting the bank could hold rates steady for some time after an August hike.\par \par \uc2 In debt trading, the government's benchmark 10-year peso bond <MX10YT=RR> rose 0.488 of a point in price to bid 93.751, pushing its yield down 8 basis points to 8.73 percent.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices <CLc1> continued their recent decline on Wednesday, now almost $30 below their all-time high set in July. Equities traders said that eased fears that high fuel costs would crimp consumer demand in the United States, Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Shares of broadcaster Televisa jumped <TLVACPO.MX> 7.15 percent to 48.09 pesos after \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  started coverage of the stock with a "buy" rating, noting the firm's growth potential from its pay TV business. Its New York-traded stock gained 6.79 percent to $24.06.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 America Movil\uc2  , the largest cell phone operator in Latin America, gained 1.38 percent to 25.66 pesos after the company said it would begin selling \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 's iPhone later this month in 10 countries within the region. Its New York-traded stock rose 1.08 percent to $51.63.\par \par \uc2 Shares of top retails \uc2 Wal-Mart de Mexico\uc2  <WALMEXV.MX> rose 2.17 percent to 41.45 pesos. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MEXICO/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080806e486001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
