\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico could step in to weaken peso - \uc2 UBS\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2008\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Aug 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has surged more than 10 percent this year and threatens to hurt the country's competitiveness, \uc2 UBS\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which share responsibility for Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, could announce a peso sale program as soon as this week, \uc2 UBS\uc2  economist Gabriel Casillas said in a report.\par \par \uc2 The government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no immediate comment.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MEX01> <MXN=> has soared in recent months as high interest rates have attracted foreign investors looking to beat paltry yields on U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Guillermo Ortiz warned last week the expensive peso could hurt Mexican exporters.\par \par \uc2 Also last week, Ortiz, asked by a reporter whether he might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, said central banks cannot vow never to use any tool available.\par \par \uc2 "He was clearly saying, 'You know what? I have no problem \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if I need to,'" Casillas said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently said it was suspending a daily sale of dollar foreign reserves, ballooning because of oil exports, that has strengthened the peso in recent years.\par \par \uc2 That is expected to reduce slightly demand for the peso, which gained to fewer than 10 to the dollar on Friday for the first time in more than five years.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the dollar sale was being suspended after the government bought $8 billion to cover \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the coming months. But traders speculated the bank wanted to stem the peso's gain.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  said in a report on Monday it does not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start selling pesos.\par \par \uc2 From 1996 to 2001, Mexico sold banks options to sell up to $250 million dollars a month to Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a program that could easily be revived, Casillas said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by central banks can become expensive, economists warn.\par \par \uc2 "It would be unwise to take any move that could be read by the markets as trying to draw a line in the sand or defend a particular level," said Gray Newman, an economist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  in New York. (Reporting by Noel Randewich; Editing by Dan Grebler) (Additional reporting by Luis Rojas)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-PESO/|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080807e484002pc\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreig